urer's and although the reviews  weren't quite as abysmal as they had  been for most of his recent efforts they  weren't exactly good that's not totally  surprising after earth was originally  pitched to Shyamalan by Will Smith as a  star vehicle for himself and his sudden  Jaden and follows the pair's they  struggle for survival after being  shipwrecked on an alien planet it's a  promising set up for the Shyamalan  treatment but the surprising lack of  chemistry between the real-life father  and son leaves an emotional void that  the movie struggles to overcome for his  part Shyamalan once again drops the ball  when it comes to the film staging and  visual elements wasting the talents of  brilliant cinematographer Peters who  shitski  along the way though after earth bombed  hard stateside it did well enough  overseas to turn a modest profit still  given his track record with tentpole  fare we're betting it'll be a while  before Shyamalan goes this big again  after giving his fan base cause for  concern with Lady in the water  Shyamalan continued his stumble with the  happening a sci-fi thriller that follows  a teacher his wife and their friends as  they try to outrun a mysterious plague  on paper the concept has the makings of  another intriguing Twilight Zone ish  tail for Shyamalan but the film features  career worst performances from Mark  Wahlberg and Zooey Deschanel a third act  that can only be described as  mind-boggling ly stupid and the sort of  hackneyed tin eared writing that leaves  one wondering how the happening got off  the ground at all my name is Elliott  Moore just going to talk in a very  positive manner giving off good vibes  and there's a reason why this movie  feels unpolished Shyamalan was working  on the script while the 2007 writers  strike loomed over Hollywood fearing a  lengthy content drought Studios began  fast-tracking productions to fill a  potential void and the happen  was one of them it was released to some  of the worst reviews 